-- resolve_topic(phrase, context): the topic a prompt is about.
--
-- ONE ELECTION, ONE KEY ORDER. chat(), converse() and converse_walk() all orient
-- through prompt_coherence() on the identical sort key, with the stated invariant
-- that the three "cannot disagree about what a prompt is about". resolve_topic is
-- the FOURTH orientation path -- it is what recall() resolves through (recall.c
-- spi_resolve_topic) -- and it disagreed with all three. The elector was already
-- built, compiled and correct; recall() just never called it.
--
-- WHAT ACTUALLY DECIDED THE TOPIC, measured: not resolve_last_word() but
-- resolve_phrase(). That function is a longest-span-first, LEFTMOST-wins span
-- resolver (content_resolve.c: `for L = n..1` outer, i ascending inner, first
-- stored span wins) -- so on any prompt where no long span is stored it descends
-- to single words and returns the leftmost one that happens to be a stored
-- entity. `resolve_phrase('What is a pawn in chess?')` = `What`;
-- `resolve_phrase('what is rain')` = `what`. resolve_last_word was almost never
-- reached, and on that same question returns `QUESTION MARK`.
--
-- So the election cannot sit behind resolve_phrase -- that is where it was first
-- placed, and it was dead code for every multi-word prompt containing any known
-- word, which is all of them. It has to come first.
--
-- ORDER OF RESOLUTION, and why:
--   1. the specificity election -- the same call and the same key order as
--      chat()/converse()/converse_walk(), so all four now agree by construction.
--   2. resolve_phrase() -- reached only when the election is silent. This is NOT
--      a demotion: measured, the election is silent on exactly the inputs that
--      ARE an entity ('pawn', 'ice cream', 'New York', 'carbon dioxide' all
--      return specificity 0 with no peers), because a phrase that resolves whole
--      has no token pair to be coherent across. Identity still wins where
--      identity exists; the election only speaks when there are competing tokens.
--   3. resolve_last_word() -- unchanged, and still the last resort.
--
-- WHY specificity > 0 GATES THE ELECTION: specificity is coherence over the
-- candidate's own total mass, so it is 0 for every token when no pair of tokens
-- shares a rated edge -- an unseeded domain, not a wrong answer. Measured:
-- 'will it rain in nashville in the next seven days' returns specificity 0 for
-- ALL nine candidate tokens (the graph holds no edge among rain/nashville/
-- weather -- no such source is seeded), while 'What is a pawn in chess?' returns
-- pawn 0.0441, chess 0.0363, and 0 for a/in. Without the gate the tiebreaks
-- alone would decide the all-zero prompt, and they rank `next` (denote_mu
-- 1391.2) above `rain` (1169.7), with `in` and `will` tied against it -- an
-- arbitrary token dressed up as a decision. With the gate, a no-signal prompt
-- falls through unchanged and the election only ever fires when the graph
-- actually said something.
--
-- The honest consequence, stated so nobody re-derives it as a bug: 'what is
-- rain' still resolves to `what`, because rain's domain is unseeded and the
-- election has nothing to say. That is a seeding gap, not a defect in this
-- body, and it resolves itself the moment a source rates an edge on rain.
--
-- NOT PARALLEL SAFE: prompt_coherence() is `LANGUAGE C STABLE` with no parallel
-- marking, so this body cannot claim more than its callee. recall.c invokes this
-- as a single scalar SPI select, where parallelism was never in play.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION resolve_topic(p_phrase text, p_context bytea)
    RETURNS bytea
    LANGUAGE sql STABLE
    SET search_path = @extschema@, public AS $$
    SELECT CASE
        WHEN p_phrase IS NULL OR btrim(p_phrase) = '' THEN p_context
        -- Literal content id (incl. a FEN rewritten to hex by the app resolve
        -- hook, GH #575). Same arm resolve_ref already has — without it a
        -- hex prompt falls through to resolve_phrase and hashes the digits.
        WHEN btrim(p_phrase) ~ '^[0-9a-f]{32}$' THEN decode(btrim(p_phrase), 'hex')
        WHEN p_context IS NOT NULL
             AND btrim(lower(p_phrase), ' ?.!') ~ '^(it|its|that|this|they|their|them|those|these|one|he|she|him|her)$'
            THEN p_context
        ELSE COALESCE(
            (SELECT y.tok
               FROM @extschema@.prompt_coherence(p_phrase) y
              WHERE y.tok IS NOT NULL
                AND y.specificity > 0
              ORDER BY y.specificity DESC NULLS LAST,
                       y.rel_mass    DESC NULLS LAST,
                       y.peers       DESC,
                       y.ord         DESC,
                       y.denote_mu   DESC NULLS LAST,
                       y.synset_id
              LIMIT 1),
            @extschema@.resolve_phrase(p_phrase),
            @extschema@.resolve_last_word(p_phrase))
    END
$$;
